Yes. That **“how many valid solutions can you invent under changing constraints?”** loop could be one of the strongest things in the app because it turns prompting itself into the game.

I’d make the iOS app feel like three products sharing the same Freak identity:

### 1. Party

The Jackbox layer.

You open the app and immediately see:

**JOIN PARTY**
`Scan QR` · `Enter code`

Inside a room, your phone dynamically becomes whatever controller the current game needs: text prompt, drawing pad, voting screen, character builder, secret objective, joystick, camera, etc.

Your Freak is already attached to your profile, so joining a party can be one tap.

### 2. Green Room

The creative studio.

This is where you make:

* characters
* stand-up sets
* voices
* scenes
* worlds
* scenario packs
* clips

Basically your existing Green Room, but mobile-native and extremely fast.

You could have an almost TikTok-like creation flow:

> **What are we making?**
> Character · Joke · Scene · World

Then ramble/type/draw → Freak Town generates it → tweak → publish/use in games.

### 3. Challenges

This is probably the **daily retention engine**.

Not real-time party play. More like Chess.com correspondence games + Wordle + creative combat.

You get a notification:

> **Tom challenged you.**
> SURVIVE THE TSUNAMI
> Constraint: Land mammals only
> 12 hours remaining.

You create:

> RACCOON
> scuba mask made from coconut shells
> ties itself to a floating refrigerator

Then the game **simulates it**.

Your friend submits theirs.

You both get the reveal simultaneously.

That is excellent.

