# Mutation is especially addictive

Don't always create from scratch.

Give the player something they've grown attached to.

Day 1:

> Create a creature capable of surviving a flood.

You make **Barry**, an amphibious raccoon.

Day 2:

> Barry's habitat is now -20°C.

You get **one mutation**.

Day 3:

> Barry's main food source disappears.

One mutation.

Day 4:

> A new predator arrives.

One mutation.

After 30 days you've got some horrific creature with:

* webbed feet
* giant fat layer
* venomous tail
* night vision
* symbiotic fungus
* pathological anxiety

And **Barry has a history**.

That gives you the Tamagotchi/Pokémon attachment loop on top of the creative game.

