# One particularly strong rule

I would avoid having an LLM simply output:

> Creativity score: 8.7

whenever possible.

For games, use **observable consequences**.

Don't tell me:

> Your raccoon solution scored 83%.

Show me the tsunami arrive.

Show the raccoon climbing.

Show its snorkel break.

Show it get swept into a hotel swimming pool.

Then:

> **SURVIVED**

That is infinitely more satisfying.

The AI judge can operate underneath, but the **result should be dramatized**.

And that gives Freak Town its visual identity: every answer becomes a tiny story.

The core product could almost be summarized as:

> **Freak Town turns imagination into something you can play against.**

That feels much bigger than just “learn prompting.”
